; Network-effect boundary for the reviewed Go declarations a host
; selects.
;
; The protected declarations are not authored in this policy. They come
; from the reviewed declaration-selection document it imports, so the
; released policy ID runs unchanged for every repository and an
; unconfigured run fails activation instead of passing vacuously.
; Purity is never inferred from a function name, a file name, a comment, or an
; unqualified annotation.
;
; Activation
; ----------
; 1. The reviewed Go model is already shipped: the embedded
;    `bifrost.go.stdlib.net-http` pack declares `bifrost.network_io` on
;    `net/http.Get` at its written arity one, and the sibling
;    `bifrost.go.stdlib.net-http-declarations` pack publishes that exact
;    package function so the Go resolver can bind it. Unlike the JavaScript,
;    TypeScript and Python rows there is no separate file to install under
;    `.bifrost/semantic-models/`: Go publishes one `net/http` declaration
;    surface, and a second activated pack declaring the same package would make
;    the overlay lookup ambiguous and fail closed for every `net/http` call.
; 2. Write the reviewed declaration selection to
;    `.bifrost/effect-boundaries/go-network-io.rqlp`:
;      (declaration-selection-document
;        :schema-version 1
;        :language go
;        :declarations [
;          (rql (enclosing-decl (function :name "Total")))])
;    Each entry is one exact `enclosing-decl` selector of a function, method,
;    or class with an exact `:name`, optionally inside one exactly named
;    owner (`inside-decl`). The document admits no other constraint and no
;    nested file reference. A missing, empty, malformed, wrong-kind or
;    wrong-language document fails activation (`policy-validation-failed`),
;    and the imported selection is part of the run's `policy_hash`. A host
;    that scans untrusted repositories owns this path: it writes its reviewed
;    document there and never runs the repository's own copy.
; 3. Enable the policy by its ID; it is opt-in and never joins a default
;    run: `bifrost --policy-id
;    bifrost.effects.go.selected-boundary-no-network-io --fail-on error`.
;
; API choice: `net/http.Get` at its written arity one. It is the
; package-function route, which the Go import binder proves by expanding the
; call site's `http` qualifier to the `net/http` import path before the
; declaration overlay is consulted, so the identity never rests on the
; spelling `Get`. `(*http.Client).Do` would bind through the concrete-receiver
; route instead, but it needs a receiver whose `*http.Client` type the analyzer
; must first agree on, so the package function is the simpler exact identity.
;
; The rule body is shared across languages; only the language label, the
; activated model, and the imported selection differ.
(policy
  :schema-version 1
  :id "bifrost.effects.go.selected-boundary-no-network-io"
  :name "Selected Go boundary reaches no network effect"
  :message "the selected Go boundary reaches the declared network effect"
  :severity error
  :description "No explicitly selected Go declaration may reach a declared network effect, directly or through workspace helpers. The effect is declared by a reviewed semantic model on the exact external API identity, never inferred from a function name, a file name, a comment, or an unqualified annotation. The protected declarations come from the reviewed declaration-selection document `.bifrost/effect-boundaries/go-network-io.rqlp`; a missing or invalid document fails activation instead of passing."
  :help-uri "https://bifrost.brokk.ai/static-analysis-policies/#network-effect-boundary"
  :tags ["effects" "network" "boundary" "go"]
  :analysis
    (analysis
      :type assertion
      ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
      ; Declaration selection: imported, never authored here. `effect` reads
      ; the procedure effects of exactly the declarations `selected` binds,
      ; so the two cannot drift apart and the policy derives no effect
      ; closure for a declaration it did not select.
      ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
      (bind :name selected
        :query (declaration-selection-file
          :path ".bifrost/effect-boundaries/go-network-io.rqlp"
          :language go))
      (bind :name effect
        :query (procedure-effects-of :binding selected))
      (join :left selected :right effect :on ((id procedure_id)))
      (group :name selected-boundary :by (selected.id)
        (aggregate :name network-effects :op count
          :where ((effect.effect_id eq "bifrost.network_io")
                  (effect.derivation eq declared))))
      (assert :group selected-boundary :value network-effects :cardinality (exactly 0))))
